      {
        "id": 30520,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-05-17T03:42:05.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Matchstickman&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Matchstickman\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I’m not a big fan of the Promo Wraith but isn’t part of the usefulness of the power the ability to <span class=\"bbcode-i\">discard</span> an environment card? If you have no Flesh of the Sun God then each hero taking 7 fire damage from Volcanic Eruption becomes a problem, you can avoid that with one use of a power… a power that can’t be discard through any card the villain might play.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Agreed.</p>\n<p>Though I agree that Stealth is far more generally useful, the main advantage of Sleuth is to skip the worst environment cards.</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:04:28.168Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
