      {
        "id": 30528,
        "name": "McBehrer",
        "username": "McBehrer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/{size}/1850_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-05-17T17:54:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I would agree that until Sleuth lets you not play a card but not discard it either, it is basically useless.</p>\n<p>But, if the next card is, say, something that would severely cripple your team like Self-Destruct Sequence or Pervasive Red Dust, discarding it can be immensely useful. Also, if it’s something that increases damage done but can be destroyed at the beginning of the environment turn, the heroes would benefit from it without letting the villains get in on it too.</p>\n<p>Still, those are very rare, specific cases, so overall stealth is far superior; especially since you can use Visionary to do the same thing, but better.</p>",
        "post_number": 28,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:04:28.681Z",
